  partName: Intake Manifold (2)
  description: The Intake Manifold (2) is a large, complex component positioned at
    the middle-center-center of the engine, constructed from metal-bright material.
    Its primary function is to distribute air-fuel mixture to the cylinders, ensuring
    efficient combustion and engine performance. Interestingly, the intake manifold's
    complex shape and large size allow for optimized airflow and fuel distribution,
    resulting in improved engine power output, fuel efficiency, and reduced emissions.
